'''
This module serves as a data acquisition 
engine that interfaces with the YouTube Data API v3. It automates the 
extraction of video metadata and comment threads for specific channels, 
applying an exponential backoff strategy to handle rate limits and quota 
restrictions gracefully. To ensure reproducibility and support offline analysis, 
the module persists all raw API responses as JSON files in data/raw/ before processing them.

The primary entry point, build_dataset(), orchestrates the full pipeline: it filters for videos 
published in a target year, parses complex ISO 8601 durations into seconds, and joins comment-level 
data with video attributes like narration type (AI vs. Human) and genre. The final output is a "tidy" 
master dataset saved to data/processed/master_dataset.csv, providing a clean, flat structure ready for 
immediate downstream analytics and machine learning.
'''
